{"archetypes":[{"name":"waterfall-state","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff rewires multi-vendor dispatch, no-fallback drops, static counts, and threshold accounting across several shell scripts.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether static and dynamic reviewer slot accounting stays consistent from dispatch-panel.sh through review-core.sh and check-reviewer-failure-threshold.sh. Pay special attention to dropped no-fallback peers, phase2 or phase3 failures, both-vendor versus single-vendor paths, and whether any static archetype can silently disappear. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prompt-trust","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes prompt rendering and scout validation for untrusted plan, feature, and diff payloads.","prompt_body":"Review the prompt-boundary changes for injection or delimiter-confusion risks introduced by rendering plan and feature context, especially the reviewer-testing exception and redaction-plus-escaping pipeline. Check whether scout dynamic archetype validation rejects unsafe generated prompt text without blocking valid specialists. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-hygiene","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes which reviewer outputs and sidecars are logged or excluded, including static Codex versus dynamic Codex artifacts.","prompt_body":"Examine run-log artifact inclusion and exclusion rules for static Codex specialist outputs, dynamic Codex twins, phased fallback outputs, metadata sidecars, and dirty-tree recovery artifacts. Look for cases where sensitive raw reviewer output could be committed or where forensic artifacts needed for debugging are accidentally dropped. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-dataflow","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The implementation adds complex bash parsing of env files, TSV, NDJSON, arrays, and status files under set -euo pipefail.","prompt_body":"Audit the new shell dataflow for quoting, word-splitting, basename normalization, jq failure behavior, blank-line record parsing, and array expansion mistakes. Focus on bugs that would only appear with unusual paths, empty files, malformed dispatcher output, or reviewer names containing expected suffix variants. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
